  "notes": [
    "No Senegalese statute or official gazette was reachable: every public holiday comes from a secondary source (Wikipedia) and is a draft. The statute that sets them was not found.",
    "The Muslim festivals (Korite, Tabaski, Maouloud, Tamkharit) and the Grand Magal of Touba depend on the moon and are declared each year; no declaration was fetched, so none is listed and a year has none until its declaration is added.",
    "A holiday that falls on a Sunday is kept on its own day: no rule of observance was confirmed.",
    "The regions and their ISO 3166-2 codes are read from a secondary copy of the ISO table, not from the official gazette; the 14 regions are those the table lists after the creation of Kaffrine, Kedougou and Sedhiou.",
    "No department list is bundled: the department is free text.",
    "No identifier format was found in a fetched source: every scheme is free text.",
    "No statutory return is listed: no fetched Senegalese source gives a due day (DGID pages name the returns but not their dates)."
  ],
